  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat's version of YouTube-DL is out of date yet again after their new release today. Or actually, I guess I should say it's now further out of date, because it has already been out of date for about a month or two now. \n\nWhile the old update a month ago only broke half the videos you could play (seems like anything that had any kind of country or music copyright of any kind wouldn't play) this new update has now broken and prevented all new videos from playing.\n\nIt always takes you guys weeks to update this stuff, sometimes, like in this case, it takes well over a month, we may even get to 2 months at this point if it keeps up.. This is unacceptable considering how absurdly easy this is to fix, to the point where users can actually do it themselves, but it'll only fix it for them locally. Why do you guys take weeks, sometimes months, to put the new Youtube-dl.exe into the folder to replace the old Youtube-dl.exe? It is a process that takes less than 5 minutes, yet here we are months later and it is still not fixed.\n\nWhy do you guys do hotfixes for other issues, but not this one? Why do we have to wait until the new patch comes out every single time to be able to watch videos again? \n\nThe last time YouTube-DL was actually up to date in VRChat was early to mid June. We are now about to enter August. I know you'll say that there's already a patch in open beta that will eventually be coming live to fix it, but that patch has been in open beta for weeks, and now that youtube-dl has broken again today, needs to be fixed again for that patch.\n\nI'm so, so, so tired of having to stop watching videos for an ENTIRE MONTH because you guys can't replace a damn .exe in a folder and push a hotfix.\n\nIt's not like watching YouTube videos is some fringe thing that only a few people in this game do too. If you look at every single popular comfy map, they all have video players in them. Stop screwing us over for weeks or months at a time. Either update it faster, or make it so that it auto-updates whenever YouTube-DL releases a new version.",
